  "rationale": "The one home (SPEC_STANDARD 15.4) of every policy value that generated code reads: typed constants of one deterministic provider module, because the Factory data/code seam (SPEC_STANDARD 15.9) gives a generator an access signature and never a value, and an address in a note is not dereferenced (SPEC_STANDARD 15.3.1). Each value is decided in the State 2 decision named by source_refs and written here once. Release ceilings are one scalar constant each (A20 rule 1, owner 2026-10-03). The trapped entry points are written out for release v1, CPython 3.12 (A03 rule 4, A20 rule 3): SANDBOX_TRAPPED_FUNCTIONS raise on any call, SANDBOX_TRAPPED_WITHOUT_ARGUMENT only when called without an argument, every method of SANDBOX_TRAPPED_CLASS raises, and SANDBOX_UNSEEDED_CONSTRUCTOR raises when constructed without a seed or with None. INSTANCE_SETTABLE_HEADER_NAMES is the part of KERNEL_SET_HEADER_NAMES an instance's required headers may name, the instance's value then sent instead of the kernel's; the credential header may name none of KERNEL_SET_HEADER_NAMES (A08 rule 5, A09 rule 1, A10 rule 7, owner 2026-10-03). SERVICE_ID_PATTERN is anchored at both ends with \\Z, so it decides the whole service_id under re.match and re.search alike (A08 rule 1). Closed sets that belong to a model - disclosure and effect classes, statuses, reasons, HTTP methods - are models enumerations, ordered by their declared order where State 1 orders them; the field names of a manifest record are the fields of its model. Neither repeats here. What code reads about the members of such an enumeration is a correspondence over that taxonomy (SPEC_STANDARD 15.2) and lives here as a version 2 record_tuple keyed by the enumeration and total over its members, so a member added without its row stops the build (60_contracts.md decision 33): EXECUTION_STATUS_CONCLUSIONS gives every NodeExecutionStatus the NodeConclusion it concludes (A13 rules 5 and 7), NODE_CONCLUSION_EFFECTS says of every NodeConclusion whether it lets a run that has ended succeed and whether it makes its dependants upstream_failed (A13 rules 5 and 7), WAIT_REASON_RESTING_STATUSES gives every WaitReason the RunStatus a run rests in while an element waits for it (A13 rule 8), and HTTP_METHOD_BODIES says of every HttpMethod whether its request carries the inputs in a body (A09 rule 2). EDGE_DELIVERY_RULES is the total relation over the three boolean facts A13 rule 9 gives an edge and yields its EdgeDelivery; keeping it in the deterministic provider prevents its rows from entering the run_graph prompt (decision 47). A cell of an enumeration column names a member; the member's home stays the enumeration. The MCP entrance's path, the protocol version answered to initialize and the server's name and version are release v1 values of 60_contracts.md decision 22 (owner, 2026-10-10). Release v1 pins the sandbox interpreter, the bubblewrap version and the kernel's one third-party package, pydantic, and names the host paths the sandbox binds read-only (60_contracts.md decision 25, owner 2026-10-10); and the names of the store's content-addressed and spool areas inside data_directory (decision 25). SANDBOX_ROOT_SYMLINKS (decision 29) are the links a usr-merged runtime needs inside the sandbox's new root: the interpreter's loader is named under /lib64, which binding /usr alone does not provide. SANDBOX_PROC_MOUNT (decision 40) is where bubblewrap mounts the environment's own proc, named once so the parent mounts it and the runner lists it at the same path. RELEASE_CEILING_JSON_DEPTH_MAX (decision 42, A20 json_depth_max) bounds the depth of every JSON value the kernel reads; it is a ceiling like the others, one scalar, never raised by a request. MCP_CATALOGUE_OPERATIONS and MCP_TOOL_INPUT_SCHEMAS (60_contracts.md decision 58) are what tools/list answers: the State 5 catalogue order, and each operation's schema as JSON text, built by experiments/cabinet-kernel/build_tool_schemas.py from the request models.",
